{
 "help": "usage: wgsextract extract region [-h] --target {mt,y,ymt,autox} [--formats LIST] [--poz]\n                                 [--y-scope SCOPE] [--ybrowse]\n\noptions:\n  -h, --help            show this help message and exit\n  --target {mt,y,ymt,autox}\n                        Region to extract: mt (chrM), y (chrY), ymt (chrY and chrM) or autox\n                        (autosomes and chrX).\n  --formats LIST        Comma-separated formats to write: fasta (consensus sequence), bam (reads)\n                        and vcf (variant calls), e.g. bam,vcf.\n  --poz                 With --target y and the bam format: restrict the BAM's Y reads to the\n                        bundled CombBED/McDonald/Poznik union (GRCh37, GRCh38 or T2T).\n  --y-scope SCOPE       Y contigs to read: primary (chrY only) or associated (also the reference's\n                        qualified Y-associated contigs, as WGS Extract v4 did; GRCh38\n                        chrY_KI270740v1_random). Written as <input>_..._associated.\n  --ybrowse             With --target y and the vcf format: call installed, allele-annotated\n                        yBrowse SNP targets (GRCh38 only; no downloads) into\n                        <input>_Y_ybrowse.vcf.gz instead.\n\nglobal options:\n  -i/--input, -o/--outdir, --genome, --ref, -t/--threads, -m/--memory, --json, --quiet, --debug,\n  --config and the other global options are accepted before or after the command; 'wgsextract\n  --help' lists them all.\n\nexamples:\n  wgsextract extract region --input sample.cram --target ymt --formats bam,vcf\n  wgsextract extract region --input sample.cram --target mt --formats fasta\n  wgsextract extract region --input sample.cram --target autox --formats vcf,fasta\n\noutputs (in the output directory unless noted):\n  Per chosen format: <input stem>_mtDNA|Y|Y_MT|autosomes_X.bam (+ .bai),\n  <input stem>_MT|Y|Y_MT|autosomes_X.vcf.gz (+ .tbi) and .fasta.\n\nneeds:\n  samtools; depending on options and inputs, also: bcftools, bgzip, tabix;\n  hours on a 30x genome.\n",
